# Transaction Monitoring Pipeline

Real-time transaction monitoring pipeline: Rust services (Axum + rdkafka)
producing/consuming Kafka-compatible events via Redpanda, flagged for
fraud heuristics, stored in ClickHouse, visualized in Grafana.

## Quick start (any machine with Docker installed)

\`\`\`bash
git clone <your-repo-url>
cd transaction-pipeline/docker
docker compose up -d --build
\`\`\`

- Send a transaction: `POST http://localhost:3001/transactions`
- Grafana dashboards: http://localhost:3000 (admin/admin)
- Prometheus: http://localhost:9090
- ClickHouse: `docker exec -it clickhouse clickhouse-client`

## Corporate/restrictive network note

If your network blocks plain HTTP apt access (common on locked-down
corporate networks), see `docker/base-images/` for a pre-patched base
image workaround, wired in via `docker/.env` (git-ignored, machine-local).
Not needed on most networks, including standard Docker Desktop setups.